2026-10-10T01:45:16.5492540Z         bridge's discovery lockfile).
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5492858Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5493375Z         <b>0.4.6</b> � newer-IDE compatibility: removed the last deprecated-API
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5494083Z         usages (terminal-process listener + provider-chooser dialog). Plugin Verifier
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5495175Z         reports no internal / scheduled-for-removal / deprecated API usage on 2025.2.
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5495816Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5496462Z         <b>0.4.5</b> � reverted the experimental 0.4.4 <code>getTerminalOutput</code>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5497165Z         tool: the terminal API it used is not stable across IDE versions and caused
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5497858Z         errors on some builds. Everything else is unchanged from 0.4.3.
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5498287Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5498793Z         <b>0.4.3</b> � the <code>@</code>-mention symbol completion now covers
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5499476Z         <b>methods/functions</b> too (not just classes) � type a method name to
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5500248Z         reference the file where it's defined.
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5500585Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5501086Z         <b>0.4.2</b> � the <code>@</code>-mention popup now includes project class
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5501718Z         symbols (type a class name to reference the file where it's defined),
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5502330Z         alongside <code>@selection</code>/<code>@diagnostics</code> and files.
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5502768Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5503284Z         <b>0.4.1</b> � expanded the plugin description / what's-new (no functional
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5503769Z         change since 0.4.0).
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5504045Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5504409Z         <b>0.4.0</b> � VS Code feature parity.
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5504731Z         <ul>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5505213Z           <li>Multi-conversation <b>tabs</b> (one agent per tab, resume across restarts).</li>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5506071Z           <li><b>Approval modes</b> (<code>/auto</code>�<code>/bypass</code>�<code>/normal</code>)
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5507006Z               and <b>extended thinking</b> (<code>/think</code>�<code>/ultrathink</code>�<code>/think-off</code>),
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5507876Z               plus <code>/new</code> <code>/stop</code> <code>/cost</code> <code>/context</code>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5508544Z               <code>/plan</code> <code>/approve</code> <code>/reject</code>.</li>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5509198Z           <li><b>Interactive plan &amp; approval cards</b> (Approve/Deny buttons).</li>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5510305Z           <li>Editor <b>Explain / Refactor</b> actions, <code>@file#L</code> reference
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5511035Z               insertion (<code>Ctrl/Cmd+Alt+K</code>), and an <code>@</code>-mention popup.</li>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5511856Z           <li>Native diff "<b>Request changes�</b>" with inline notes, and batch
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5512405Z               <b>openMultiDiff</b> multi-file review.</li>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5512910Z           <li><b>In-editor app preview</b> (JCEF) with Start/Stop.</li>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5661374Z           <li>Live context-window indicator; new-chat / reopen-closed shortcuts.</li>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5661919Z         </ul>
2026-10-10T01:45:16.5674003Z     ]' tag will be set to '<b>[0.4.158] - Pair with CLI model review and diagnostic evidence (2026-10-09)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.96</code> after its public npm release and this extension's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Keep Doctor and upgrade prompts aligned with the paired CLI recommendation.</li><li>Retain the compatibility floor and runtime capability diagnostics; experimental native review and durable Windows/macOS recovery remain outside release acceptance.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.157] - Pair with strict settings write fairness (2026-10-08)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.94</code> after its public npm release and this plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Keep Doctor and the upgrade prompt on the same current CLI recommendation, including artifacts produced by incremental builds.</li><li>Refresh the compiled recommendation and upgrade guidance for concurrent permission-rule writes while retaining the compatibility floor and live capability diagnostics.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.156] - Pair with bounded investigation recovery (2026-10-08)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.93</code>, Session Core <code>0.3.18</code>, and Context Memory Kernel <code>0.1.8</code> after their public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Refresh the compiled CLI upgrade recommendation and paired release guidance for bounded evidence investigations and organization goal services.</li><li>Repair the dependency setup used to aggregate three-platform accessibility and performance evidence without changing producer requirements.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.155] - Candidate runtime and restart validation fixes (2026-10-07)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.92</code> after its public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass; this entry does not establish publication.</li><li>Pair with Session Core <code>0.3.17</code> and Context/Memory Kernel <code>0.1.7<