2026-10-10T01:48:27.2082375Z         <b>0.4.26</b> � fix: no more false "???? cc CLI" when <code>cc</code> IS
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2094192Z         installed. The version probe timeout went 5s ? 12s (cold starts), and since
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2269875Z         <code>cc</code> is also the C compiler's name, the plugin now resolves the
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2298052Z         binary with fallback (<code>cc ? chainlesschain ? clc ? clchain</code>) and
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2308553Z         uses it for the chat spawn and every probe.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2327816Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2349673Z         <b>0.4.25</b> � the agent can actually ask you a question:
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2365595Z         <code>ask_user_question</code> now pops a dialog (single-choice / multi-select
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2376130Z         checkboxes / free-text input) so the agent can clarify instead of guessing.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2378127Z         Requires <code>cc</code> ? 0.162.95.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2394073Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2402877Z         <b>0.4.24</b> � fix: a graceful "couldn't ask in the panel" degradation no
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2404082Z         longer renders as a scary <b>? ask_user_question</b> failure.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2422084Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2476974Z         <b>0.4.23</b> � new <b>? LLM ? ?? cc ??�</b> menu item (check on demand),
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2488738Z         plus a clear hint when the <code>cc</code> CLI isn't installed.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2489912Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2494185Z         <b>0.4.22</b> � you're now told when a newer <code>cc</code> CLI is published
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2499744Z         on npm, so you don't silently miss new features.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2506496Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2511856Z         <b>0.4.21</b> � fix: reconfiguring the LLM now restarts the running chat so it
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2512832Z         picks up the new provider/model/key (no more "?????? / ??????").
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2513215Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2514029Z         <b>0.4.20</b> � new <code>/review</code> command: review your uncommitted git
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2514587Z         diff right from the chat (matches the VS Code panel).
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2514980Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2515500Z         <b>0.4.19</b> � fix: the suggested vision model now matches the CLI's
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2516452Z         actual default (<code>doubao-seed-2-0-lite-260215</code>) instead of an
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2516978Z         older snapshot, so the prefilled value equals what
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2517339Z         <code>cc agent --image</code> uses.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2517599Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2518023Z         <b>0.4.18</b> � dedicated image-recognition (vision) model entry: the
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2518520Z         <b>? LLM</b> button is now a small menu (configure full LLM <i>or</i> just
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2519025Z         the vision model), plus a <b>Tools ? Configure Vision Model</b> action.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2520082Z         Set <code>llm.visionModel</code> without re-running the whole wizard or
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2520566Z         re-typing your API key; blank reverts to the text model.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2520937Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2521416Z         <b>0.4.17</b> � first-run nudge: when no LLM provider is configured yet,
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2523245Z         the chat panel now shows a dim hint pointing at the <b>? LLM</b> button
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2523879Z         instead of staying blank until the first turn fails with a 401 (VS Code
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2524571Z         onboarding parity).
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2524879Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2525501Z         <b>0.4.16</b> � chat panel LLM UX: (1) paste screenshots � Ctrl/Cmd+V an
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2526262Z         image to attach it to your next message (vision); (2) a <b>? LLM</b>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2526871Z         quick-entry button by Send opens the provider/model wizard, and auth
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2528460Z         failures (401/403/missing key) now hint at it; (3) the wizard can set a
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2529808Z         separate <b>image-recognition (vision) model</b> � text and vision models
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2530861Z         no longer have to be the same.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2531679Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2532603Z         <b>0.4.15</b> � multi-line chat composer: the input now wraps across
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2533851Z         lines � <b>Enter</b> sends, <b>Shift+Enter</b> adds a newline (VS Code
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2534296Z         parity).
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2534539Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2535039Z         <b>0.4.14</b> � extended-thinking reasoning (with <code>/think</code>) now
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2535652Z         streams into the transcript dimmed/italic, set apart from the answer
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2536098Z         (VS Code parity).
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2536350Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2536856Z         <b>0.4.13</b> � Markdown rendering in the chat transcript: fenced/inline
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2537458Z         <code>code</code> (monospace) and <b>bold</b> now render instead of raw
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2538326Z         markers (VS Code parity). Streaming stays plain, then snaps to styled.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2538719Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2539202Z         <b>0.4.12</b> � "Fix with ChainlessChain" intention: on an error/warning
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2539748Z         line, Alt+Enter offers a quick-fix that seeds the chat with a fix request
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2540569Z         scoped to that file + those problems (VS Code parity).
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2540961Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2541458Z         <b>0.4.11</b> � slash-command autocomplete: typing <code>/</code> at the
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2542034Z         start of the chat input pops a chooser of the panel's commands
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2542684Z         (<code>/new</code>, <code>/compact</code>, <code>/think</code>, �),
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2543421Z         filtered as you type (VS Code parity).
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2543735Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2544166Z         <b>0.4.10</b> � fix: wrap the diff-review document reads
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2544698Z         (<code>openDiff</code>/<code>openMultiDiff</code>) in a read action.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2545290Z         Since 2026.2 the EDT no longer grants implicit read access, so building
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2546152Z         the diff threw "Read access is allowed from inside read-action only" on
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2546565Z         2026.2+. No behavior change on 2025.x.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2546861Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2547505Z         <b>0.4.9</b> � fix: the chat tool window now deterministically uses the
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2548084Z         LLM provider you configured (<code>cc config</code> / Configure LLM),
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2548672Z         reading <code>~/.chainlesschain/config.json</code> and passing it
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2549591Z         explicitly to <code>cc agent</code> � no more spurious
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2550375Z         <code>Anthropic error: 401</code> when another provider is configured.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2550837Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2551329Z         <b>0.4.8</b> � <code>/compact</code> in the chat tool window (Claude-Code
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2551936Z         IDE parity): trims the live conversation history between turns (no extra
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2552521Z         LLM call) and reports the tokens saved. Mirrors the VS Code 0.31.0
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2552945Z         feature.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2553172Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2553661Z         <b>0.4.7</b> � cleared the remaining API-compatibility flags the Plugin
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2554269Z         Verifier reported on 2026.x: the @-mention list renderer no longer uses a
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2554889Z         scheduled-for-removal helper, and the deprecated terminal customizer was
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2555483Z         removed (a <code>cc</code> you run in a terminal still auto-connects via the
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2555938Z         bridge's discovery lockfile).
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2556200Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2556656Z         <b>0.4.6</b> � newer-IDE compatibility: removed the last deprecated-API
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2557273Z         usages (terminal-process listener + provider-chooser dialog). Plugin Verifier
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2557877Z         reports no internal / scheduled-for-removal / deprecated API usage on 2025.2.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2558345Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2558846Z         <b>0.4.5</b> � reverted the experimental 0.4.4 <code>getTerminalOutput</code>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2559385Z         tool: the terminal API it used is not stable across IDE versions and caused
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2559942Z         errors on some builds. Everything else is unchanged from 0.4.3.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2560334Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2560768Z         <b>0.4.3</b> � the <code>@</code>-mention symbol completion now covers
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2561458Z         <b>methods/functions</b> too (not just classes) � type a method name to
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2561955Z         reference the file where it's defined.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2562272Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2562778Z         <b>0.4.2</b> � the <code>@</code>-mention popup now includes project class
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2563384Z         symbols (type a class name to reference the file where it's defined),
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2563997Z         alongside <code>@selection</code>/<code>@diagnostics</code> and files.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2564431Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2564924Z         <b>0.4.1</b> � expanded the plugin description / what's-new (no functional
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2565380Z         change since 0.4.0).
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2565648Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2566255Z         <b>0.4.0</b> � VS Code feature parity.
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2566575Z         <ul>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2567048Z           <li>Multi-conversation <b>tabs</b> (one agent per tab, resume across restarts).</li>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2567910Z           <li><b>Approval modes</b> (<code>/auto</code>�<code>/bypass</code>�<code>/normal</code>)
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2568738Z               and <b>extended thinking</b> (<code>/think</code>�<code>/ultrathink</code>�<code>/think-off</code>),
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2569458Z               plus <code>/new</code> <code>/stop</code> <code>/cost</code> <code>/context</code>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2570074Z               <code>/plan</code> <code>/approve</code> <code>/reject</code>.</li>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2572575Z           <li><b>Interactive plan &amp; approval cards</b> (Approve/Deny buttons).</li>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2573275Z           <li>Editor <b>Explain / Refactor</b> actions, <code>@file#L</code> reference
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2573898Z               insertion (<code>Ctrl/Cmd+Alt+K</code>), and an <code>@</code>-mention popup.</li>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2575009Z           <li>Native diff "<b>Request changes�</b>" with inline notes, and batch
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2575737Z               <b>openMultiDiff</b> multi-file review.</li>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2576175Z           <li><b>In-editor app preview</b> (JCEF) with Start/Stop.</li>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2576741Z           <li>Live context-window indicator; new-chat / reopen-closed shortcuts.</li>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2577183Z         </ul>
2026-10-10T01:48:27.2592792Z     ]' tag will be set to '<b>[0.4.158] - Pair with CLI model review and diagnostic evidence (2026-10-09)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.96</code> after its public npm release and this extension's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Keep Doctor and upgrade prompts aligned with the paired CLI recommendation.</li><li>Retain the compatibility floor and runtime capability diagnostics; experimental native review and durable Windows/macOS recovery remain outside release acceptance.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.157] - Pair with strict settings write fairness (2026-10-08)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.94</code> after its public npm release and this plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Keep Doctor and the upgrade prompt on the same current CLI recommendation, including artifacts produced by incremental builds.</li><li>Refresh the compiled recommendation and upgrade guidance for concurrent permission-rule writes while retaining the compatibility floor and live capability diagnostics.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.156] - Pair with bounded investigation recovery (2026-10-08)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.93</code>, Session Core <code>0.3.18</code>, and Context Memory Kernel <code>0.1.8</code> after their public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Refresh the compiled CLI upgrade recommendation and paired release guidance for bounded evidence investigations and organization goal services.</li><li>Repair the dependency setup used to aggregate three-platform accessibility and performance evidence without changing producer requirements.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.155] - Candidate runtime and restart validation fixes (2026-10-07)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.92</code> after its public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass; this entry does not establish publication.</li><li>Pair with Session Core <code>0.3.17</code> and Context/Memory Kernel <code>0.1.7</code> for current runtime and packaging fixes, and refresh paired upgrade guidance.</li><li>Disable development automatic plugin reload in the installed-ZIP UI test host, preventing Windows 2025.2 restart tests from unloading Robot server and ChainlessChain mid-journey. This changes the test host; full IDE restart validation remains required.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.154] - Pair with cross-platform CLI fixes (2026-10-06)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.91</code> after its public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Include the current IDE source changes with the Windows native evaluator compatibility fixes and refreshed Session Core and Personal Data Hub packages.</li></ul>'
