2026-10-10T01:55:55.8545799Z         <b>0.4.29 / 0.4.30</b> � fix: <b>"Configure LLM" now pre-fills your config</b>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8552420Z         � no more re-typing model+key. The wizard pre-fills your current model, base
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8557207Z         URL and vision model, pre-selects your current provider (? ??), and lets you
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8558005Z         <b>leave the API key blank to keep the stored one</b> (only required when there's
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8560582Z         no key yet or you switch providers). The config itself was never lost � it lives
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8566717Z         in <code>~/.chainlesschain/config.json</code> and survives CLI updates; the
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8590476Z         wizard just didn't pre-fill it. (Mirrors the VS Code 0.34.0 fix. 0.4.30 adds
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8616309Z         this very change-note, which 0.4.29 omitted.)
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8616889Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8643936Z         <b>0.4.28</b> � docs: the Marketplace "What's New" now lists every release
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8653131Z         (it had silently stopped at 0.4.19 � change-notes are no longer missed).
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8662109Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8666402Z         <b>0.4.27</b> � cleared the 2 deprecated-API usages the Marketplace verifier
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8667809Z         flagged (now <code>URI.toURL()</code> + a combo-box dialog), so the plugin
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8676797Z         stays compatible with future IntelliJ releases.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8694545Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8695165Z         <b>0.4.26</b> � fix: no more false "???? cc CLI" when <code>cc</code> IS
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8699356Z         installed. The version probe timeout went 5s ? 12s (cold starts), and since
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8700211Z         <code>cc</code> is also the C compiler's name, the plugin now resolves the
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8700973Z         binary with fallback (<code>cc ? chainlesschain ? clc ? clchain</code>) and
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8701628Z         uses it for the chat spawn and every probe.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8702065Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8702637Z         <b>0.4.25</b> � the agent can actually ask you a question:
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8703380Z         <code>ask_user_question</code> now pops a dialog (single-choice / multi-select
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8704183Z         checkboxes / free-text input) so the agent can clarify instead of guessing.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8704792Z         Requires <code>cc</code> ? 0.162.95.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8705186Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8705795Z         <b>0.4.24</b> � fix: a graceful "couldn't ask in the panel" degradation no
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8706942Z         longer renders as a scary <b>? ask_user_question</b> failure.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8707485Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8708080Z         <b>0.4.23</b> � new <b>? LLM ? ?? cc ??�</b> menu item (check on demand),
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8708731Z         plus a clear hint when the <code>cc</code> CLI isn't installed.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8714872Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8737425Z         <b>0.4.22</b> � you're now told when a newer <code>cc</code> CLI is published
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8763210Z         on npm, so you don't silently miss new features.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8781048Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8788702Z         <b>0.4.21</b> � fix: reconfiguring the LLM now restarts the running chat so it
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8794019Z         picks up the new provider/model/key (no more "?????? / ??????").
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8796314Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8803303Z         <b>0.4.20</b> � new <code>/review</code> command: review your uncommitted git
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8813650Z         diff right from the chat (matches the VS Code panel).
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8820958Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8824395Z         <b>0.4.19</b> � fix: the suggested vision model now matches the CLI's
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8825148Z         actual default (<code>doubao-seed-2-0-lite-260215</code>) instead of an
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8825778Z         older snapshot, so the prefilled value equals what
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8829044Z         <code>cc agent --image</code> uses.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8830934Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8834874Z         <b>0.4.18</b> � dedicated image-recognition (vision) model entry: the
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8835614Z         <b>? LLM</b> button is now a small menu (configure full LLM <i>or</i> just
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8836306Z         the vision model), plus a <b>Tools ? Configure Vision Model</b> action.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8836993Z         Set <code>llm.visionModel</code> without re-running the whole wizard or
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8837643Z         re-typing your API key; blank reverts to the text model.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8839005Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8839696Z         <b>0.4.17</b> � first-run nudge: when no LLM provider is configured yet,
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8862490Z         the chat panel now shows a dim hint pointing at the <b>? LLM</b> button
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8870115Z         instead of staying blank until the first turn fails with a 401 (VS Code
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8874490Z         onboarding parity).
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8877987Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8885205Z         <b>0.4.16</b> � chat panel LLM UX: (1) paste screenshots � Ctrl/Cmd+V an
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8888956Z         image to attach it to your next message (vision); (2) a <b>? LLM</b>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8892886Z         quick-entry button by Send opens the provider/model wizard, and auth
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8904701Z         failures (401/403/missing key) now hint at it; (3) the wizard can set a
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8965242Z         separate <b>image-recognition (vision) model</b> � text and vision models
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8967212Z         no longer have to be the same.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8968194Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8969451Z         <b>0.4.15</b> � multi-line chat composer: the input now wraps across
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8970789Z         lines � <b>Enter</b> sends, <b>Shift+Enter</b> adds a newline (VS Code
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8971861Z         parity).
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8972560Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8973646Z         <b>0.4.14</b> � extended-thinking reasoning (with <code>/think</code>) now
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8974764Z         streams into the transcript dimmed/italic, set apart from the answer
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8975811Z         (VS Code parity).
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8976497Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8977589Z         <b>0.4.13</b> � Markdown rendering in the chat transcript: fenced/inline
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8978763Z         <code>code</code> (monospace) and <b>bold</b> now render instead of raw
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8980033Z         markers (VS Code parity). Streaming stays plain, then snaps to styled.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8980905Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8988917Z         <b>0.4.12</b> � "Fix with ChainlessChain" intention: on an error/warning
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8990236Z         line, Alt+Enter offers a quick-fix that seeds the chat with a fix request
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8991445Z         scoped to that file + those problems (VS Code parity).
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8992238Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8993329Z         <b>0.4.11</b> � slash-command autocomplete: typing <code>/</code> at the
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8994373Z         start of the chat input pops a chooser of the panel's commands
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8995533Z         (<code>/new</code>, <code>/compact</code>, <code>/think</code>, �),
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8996422Z         filtered as you type (VS Code parity).
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8997192Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8998027Z         <b>0.4.10</b> � fix: wrap the diff-review document reads
2026-10-10T01:55:55.8999020Z         (<code>openDiff</code>/<code>openMultiDiff</code>) in a read action.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9000013Z         Since 2026.2 the EDT no longer grants implicit read access, so building
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9002124Z         the diff threw "Read access is allowed from inside read-action only" on
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9002855Z         2026.2+. No behavior change on 2025.x.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9003609Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9004289Z         <b>0.4.9</b> � fix: the chat tool window now deterministically uses the
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9005087Z         LLM provider you configured (<code>cc config</code> / Configure LLM),
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9005871Z         reading <code>~/.chainlesschain/config.json</code> and passing it
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9006671Z         explicitly to <code>cc agent</code> � no more spurious
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9007462Z         <code>Anthropic error: 401</code> when another provider is configured.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9008096Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9009048Z         <b>0.4.8</b> � <code>/compact</code> in the chat tool window (Claude-Code
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9009900Z         IDE parity): trims the live conversation history between turns (no extra
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9010718Z         LLM call) and reports the tokens saved. Mirrors the VS Code 0.31.0
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9011368Z         feature.
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9011764Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T01:55:55.9012431Z         <b>0.4.7</b> � cleared the remaining API-compatibility flags the Plugin
